        "writtenLesson": "Act I: The Cold Open — Intuition Kills Beginners\n\nWhen choosing a business path, human beings are terrible at relying on \"gut feeling.\"\nOur gut is easily seduced by aesthetic branding, daydreams of easy wealth, or the enthusiastic advice of a friend who knows nothing about commerce.\n\nTo make an unassailable commercial choice, you must replace emotional intuition with a cold, numerical scorecard: The 25-Point Skill Scoring Matrix.\n\nAct II: The Five Scoring Vectors\n\nRate each skill candidate from 1 (Terrible) to 5 (World-Class) across these five dimensions:\n\n1. Commercial Demand (/5):\n   - 1 = Nobody pays for this; purely speculative or academic.\n   - 3 = Moderate consumer demand, but low willingness to pay.\n   - 5 = B2B companies are actively spending large budgets and hiring contractors right now.\n\n2. Learning Speed (/5):\n   - 1 = Requires multiple years of formal academic training or complex coding.\n   - 3 = Requires 2–3 months of intensive practice before producing acceptable output.\n   - 5 = A disciplined person can master the core software workflow in 7–14 days.\n\n3. Independent Proof (/5):\n   - 1 = Impossible to demonstrate without private corporate security clearance.\n   - 3 = Can create mockups, but hard to prove real-world utility.\n   - 5 = Can download public material and create an undeniable before-and-after demo in 3 hours.\n\n4. Prospect Access (/5):\n   - 1 = Decision-makers are cloistered behind layers of enterprise security and gatekeepers.\n   - 3 = Can reach via cold email, but open rates are low.\n   - 5 = Founders and creators are publicly active on LinkedIn, Twitter, or public email inboxes daily.\n\n5. Delivery Predictability (/5):\n   - 1 = Scope creep is rampant; client expectations are subjective and impossible to please.\n   - 3 = Moderate revision rounds required.\n   - 5 = Scope is clearly defined by fixed deliverables (e.g., 20 edited clips, 1 landing page).\n\nAct III: Scoring Thresholds\n\n- 22–25 Points: Tier 1 Vehicle. Immediate green light. Do not hesitate; begin learning today.\n- 17–21 Points: Tier 2 Vehicle. Commercially viable, but contains minor friction in access or speed.\n- Under 16 Points: Discard immediately. High risk of getting bogged down in learning loops without cash flow.\n\nAct IV: Strategic Implementation Protocols and Battle Exercises\n\nComplete the Scorecard for Your Top 3 Skills:\n\nDraw a 5-column table on paper:\n[Skill Name] | Demand | Speed | Proof | Access | Delivery | TOTAL (/25)\n\nScore each honestly. The skill with the highest numerical score is your permanent operational vehicle for the next 90 days. Close all other tabs."
