        "writtenLesson": "Act I: The Cold Open — Time Is Your Only Capital\n\nWhen starting with ₹0, your single most scarce resource is time.\nIf you spend 6 hours researching and creating custom video samples for a prospect who has no money or no access, you have burned 25% of your working week for zero commercial return.\n\nYou cannot afford to create custom samples for everyone.\nYou must operate with an elimination mindset: ruthlessly disqualifying weak leads before you invest a single minute of production labor.\n\nIn this lesson, we deploy the Master MPA Scorecard.\n\nAct II: The Scoring Matrix\n\nEvery candidate on your prospect list is evaluated against three binary questions:\n- Factor 1 (Money): Do they have verifiable commercial revenue, an active team, and marketing spend? [Yes = 1 / No = 0]\n- Factor 2 (Problem): Do they have active long-form content with a visible short-form repurposing gap? [Yes = 1 / No = 0]\n- Factor 3 (Access): Do you have an active, verified direct communication route to the decision-maker? [Yes = 1 / No = 0]\n\nTiers:\n- Tier 1 (Score = 3/3): Triple Match. The Holy Grail. Immediate candidate for a bespoke unsolicited spec sample.\n- Tier 2 (Score = 2/3): Viable Opportunity. Worth reaching out with a standardized portfolio sample or quick Loom audit.\n- Tier 3 (Score = 1/3 or 0/3): Discard. Do not touch.\n\nAct III: Case Study Comparison\n\nCandidate A: Local Bakery Owner\n- Money: Yes (Has retail shop).\n- Problem: No (Does not record long-form content; a podcast makes no sense for them).\n- Access: Yes (Can walk into the store).\n- Score: 2/3, but Problem is zero. Discard for content repurposing.\n\nCandidate B: B2B FinTech CEO Hosting a Weekly YouTube Series\n- Money: Yes (50-person company, runs Google Ads).\n- Problem: Yes (40 episodes on YouTube, 0 Shorts published).\n- Access: Yes (Active on LinkedIn daily).\n- Score: 3/3. Triple Match. This is where you focus your energy.\n\nAct IV: Strategic Implementation Protocols and Battle Exercises\n\nConstruct Your \"Target 20 Master Prospect Roster\":\n\nOpen Google Sheets. Build a table with these columns:\n- Column A: Company Name\n- Column B: Founder / Decision-Maker Name\n- Column C: Long-Form Source URL (YouTube/Podcast link)\n- Column D: Money Score (1/0)\n- Column E: Problem Score (1/0)\n- Column F: Access Score (1/0)\n- Column G: Total MPA Score (/3)\n- Column H: Outreach Status (Ready / Sample Built / Sent / Follow-Up)\n\nPopulate this sheet with exactly 20 verified prospects who score at least 2/3 (with at least 5 scoring a perfect 3/3). This is your launch pipeline."
