        "writtenLesson": "Act I: The Cold Open — The Line Between Demonstration and Theft\n\nWhen using a founder's public podcast or interview to build a spec sample, you must operate with immaculate legal and ethical discipline.\n\nThere is a vast, vital difference between:\n- Creating a private speculative demonstration to show a prospective client what you can do for them.\n- Illegally downloading their content, publishing it on your own public social media accounts without permission, and trying to monetize their brand.\n\nIf you cross that line, you are not an ambitious operator; you are a content pirate who will get slapped with copyright strikes, account bans, and legal notices.\n\nIn this lesson, we define the ethical rules of engagement for spec work.\n\nAct II: The Golden Rules of Ethical Spec Work\n\nRule 01: Private Hosting Only\nNever publish your derivative spec clips on your public TikTok, Instagram, or YouTube channel without written permission from the creator.\nHost the sample privately:\n- An unlisted YouTube video link.\n- A view-only Google Drive or Dropbox folder.\n- A private Notion preview page.\nThe sample is a private portfolio presentation sent directly to the owner, not a public broadcast.\n\nRule 02: Total Attribution & Transparency\nInside your preview, prominently display the original source:\n\"Original Source: Episode #42 of The B2B Growth Podcast with [Host Name]. Edited as an unsolicited concept demonstration by [Your Name].\"\nNever imply that the creator commissioned the work or endorsed you.\n\nRule 03: The Instant Removal Guarantee\nIn your outreach note, include this respectful assurance:\n\"This edit was created purely as a private concept sample for your review. If you prefer that I delete this file from my drive, simply let me know and I will remove it immediately.\"\n\nAct III: What Material Should You Use?\n\nOnly use material that is publicly published for free consumption:\n- Public YouTube interviews.\n- Public podcast episodes.\n- Public keynote speeches.\nNever use content from behind a paid paywall, private membership vault, or leaked internal training call.\n\nAct IV: Strategic Implementation Protocols and Battle Exercises\n\nExecute the \"Ethical Compliance Pre-Flight Check\":\n\nBefore sending any spec sample link to a prospect, verify:\n- [ ] The video is hosted on an unlisted/private link.\n- [ ] The file name clearly says: `[Creator_Name]_Concept_Sample_by_[Your_Name].mp4`.\n- [ ] No commercial ads are enabled on the link.\n- [ ] You have recorded the source episode link and timestamp in your notes."
